  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think adding this would be extremely useful to Avatar Creators. Things such as an \"Earmuffs\" boolean in the synced Parameters when Earmuffs Mode is enabled (in a way similar to \"MuteSelf\") would be fantastic. I can use that as a way to make my own 3D model of Earmuffs to appear on my Avatar whenever I enable it.\nSecondly, you should add the Animator Parameters used for changing the Camera Resolution and Orientation as well. This would extremely help with prefabs such as VRCLens, as it currently relies on the user to have their VRCLens sensor resolution set within Unity at one resolution in order for it to actually work at a higher resolution. Adding Parameters for the Camera would help solve this issue, allowing VRCLens to automatically detect the resolution set.",
